## Common Bug Types and Solutions

### State Management Issues
```typescript
// Problem: Component not re-rendering with state updates
function BuggyCounter() {
  // Bug: Mutating state directly
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  
  const increment = () => {
    count++; // Direct mutation, won't trigger re-render
  };
  
  return <button onClick={increment}>{count}</button>;
}

// Solution: Use state setter correctly
function FixedCounter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  
  const increment = () => {
    setCount(prevCount => prevCount + 1); // Proper state update
  };
  
  return <button onClick={increment}>{count}</button>;
}
```

### Event Handling Bugs
```typescript
// Problem: Event handler using stale closure
function BuggyForm() {
  const [name, setName] = useState('');
  
  // Bug: This effect sets up a listener that captures the initial value of 'name'
  useEffect(() => {
    const handleSubmit = () => {
      console.log(`Submitting: ${name}`); // Will always use initial value
    };
    
    document.addEventListener('submit-form', handleSubmit);
    return () => document.removeEventListener('submit-form', handleSubmit);
  }, []); // Missing dependency
  
  return <input value={name} onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)} />;
}

// Solution: Include all dependencies or use ref
function FixedForm() {
  const [name, setName] = useState('');
  
  // Fix: Include name in dependency array or use a ref
  useEffect(() => {
    const handleSubmit = () => {
      console.log(`Submitting: ${name}`); // Will use current value
    };
    
    document.addEventListener('submit-form', handleSubmit);
    return () => document.removeEventListener('submit-form', handleSubmit);
  }, [name]); // Proper dependency
  
  return <input value={name} onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)} />;
}
```

## Performance Bug Fixes

### Common Performance Issues
1. Unnecessary re-renders
2. Expensive calculations in render paths
3. Memory leaks
4. Large bundle sizes
5. Inefficient API calls

### Performance Fix Example
```typescript
// Problem: Component re-rendering too often
const BuggyList = ({ items }) => {
  // Bug: New function created on every render causing child components to re-render
  const handleItemClick = (item) => {
    console.log('Item clicked:', item);
  };
  
  return (
    <div>
      {items.map(item => (
        <ListItem 
          key={item.id} 
          item={item} 
          onClick={handleItemClick} // New function reference on every render
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};

// Solution: Memoize the function with useCallback
const FixedList = ({ items }) => {
  // Fix: Stable function reference
  const handleItemClick = useCallback((item) => {
    console.log('Item clicked:', item);
  }, []);
  
  return (
    <div>
      {items.map(item => (
        <ListItem 
          key={item.id} 
          item={item} 
          onClick={handleItemClick} // Same function reference across renders
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

## Post-Fix Monitoring

### Metrics to Track
- Error rates before and after fix
- User engagement with fixed feature
- Performance metrics for affected components
- Support tickets or reports related to the issue

### Monitoring Implementation
- Add logging for edge cases that might still occur
- Set up alerts for similar patterns
- Document the fix for future reference
- Share knowledge with the team about the root cause and solution 